  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WWF Making Disaster Management sustainable</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to integrate NbS with common Climate Risk Management (CRM) approaches applied  by humanitarian- and conservation actors into a combined CRM framework that is aligned with the  cooperation agreement between WWF and the International Federation of the Red Cross and Red  Crescent (IFRC). The NLRC together with Zambia Red Cross Society and WWF NL alongside WWF Zambia, proposes to implement a 1.5 years &#x2018;proof of concept&#x2019; project to contribute to the following programme-wide objective: Immediate and long-term climate resilience of communities and their natural environment, through a more sustainable relationship between people and nature</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Zambia is in clear need of longer-term climate adaptation measures to respond to disaster risk and to build greater climate resilience for vulnerable communities. Now is the opportune moment to explore systematically how the natural system can play a role in building this climate resilience in comparison to grey infrastructure methods which have often failed in the past. This can be the foundation for  ownership on collective decision making towards NbS and catalyze on 
the increased political will  around NbS in Zambia and across the globe. Catalysing this momentum by building a flagship  programme under the Red Cross and WWF partnership can show extreme value of not only this unique  collaboration, but by building a proof of concept that can demonstrate the value of NbS in Zambia and  beyond.</narrative>
  </description>
